  "body": "Live Session intake previously reused musicians by email, provisioned credentials/roles implicitly, and saved contacts before the intake. A later failure or concurrent retry could leave unrelated accounts linked or duplicate/orphan contacts. This change saves contacts, intake, musicians, songs and a private actor/request receipt in one transaction. Exact retries have no additional effects; changed accepted payloads return 409. Explicit record reuse requires CRM access or the actor's own record, and shared email addresses remain valid for separate people. Intake creates no login credentials or roles.\n\nAll contact API creation now requires an actor-scoped request key. Web and native contact forms retain it across lost responses and field edits, resetting on completion or explicit abandonment. Older clients/imports without a key receive an update/refresh error and must use the current web form or supply a stable key. Native companion diegueins680/TDF-mobile#100 is merged; native publication remains blocked by the release guide's physical iOS Google sign-in check (the owner has no physical iOS device).\n\nThe existing rider storage uses deterministic actor/request/content paths, verifies stored bytes on retry, and blocks conflicting partial files for operator review. Failed database writes may leave a recoverable unreferenced upload; existing files are never silently overwritten. Migration 109 preserves receipts on rollback once used and adds the archived-actor guard. Its introduction commit remains in ancestry.\n\nValidation before main integration: ten PostgreSQL tests passed for shared-email false positives, concurrent retries, changed payloads, actor scope, authorized/unauthorized references, partial failure rollback, archival, rider reuse and missing keys. Unused migration rollback/reapply and refusal to destroy used receipts passed. All 109 migrations applied twice with complete schema verification against a network-isolated production restore. Eight web intake tests, six native contact tests, web/native typechecks and lint, and the catalog authority audit passed. Canonical web/mobile contracts regenerate without a mobile diff after integrating main #431. Full protected CI must pass on the exact integrated head before merge.\n\nDepends on #430, which supplies the provider identity prevention and common contact request helper. Core reconciliation #426 is already deployed and production cleanup receipts are unchanged. Guest booking/course/trial email-only reuse remains separate follow-up work; this PR does not claim that those paths or native publication are complete.\n",
